EXT. BAIL BONDS DRIVE-THRU - NIGHT

A cinderblock shack with a pneumatic tube and a speaker post. Neon: BAIL 24/7. Rain.

MARISOL, 30s, in a cardigan, sits inside behind bulletproof glass, eating cereal from a mug.

A battered hatchback pulls up. HUGO, 50s, rolls down the window and leans toward the post.

HUGO
Hi. I'd like to bail out my brother.

MARISOL
(through the speaker)
Name?

HUGO
Rodolfo.

MARISOL
Charge?

HUGO
Is "sleepwalking" a charge?

She stops chewing.

MARISOL
Sir.

HUGO
He took a municipal bus. In pajamas. Drove it to Tulsa.

DOUG (O.S.)
(over the speaker, scratchy)
Marisol, is that the sleepwalker?

MARISOL
Doug, you're on the intercom again.

DOUG (O.S.)
Tell him it's two thousand.

HUGO
Two thousand?

MARISOL
He said that on purpose.

DOUG (O.S.)
I did.

Hugo pulls out a fistful of crumpled bills. Counts. Frowns. Looks up.

HUGO
I have eleven hundred.

MARISOL
Leave your watch.

HUGO
It's my father's watch.

DOUG (O.S.)
Then leave your car.

HUGO
Then how do I take him home?

A long beat. Marisol sets the mug down. Presses the tube button. A canister whooshes toward Hugo's window.

MARISOL
Sign the form.
